## 🔍 Detailed Analysis

### Revenue Analysis
Total Revenue reached ₹2.35 Cr, showing an increase of 18.6% compared to the previous period. Sales trends indicate steady business growth and increasing market demand.

### Order Performance
Total Orders reached 23,456, representing a growth of 14.8%. The increase suggests improved customer engagement and higher transaction volume.

### Product Analysis
Apple iPhone 13 emerged as the highest revenue-generating product. Other strong-performing products included Samsung Galaxy S21 and Boat Headphones.

### Category Analysis
Electronics contributed 25.5% of total revenue, making it the top-performing category. Clothing contributed 24.5%, while Home & Kitchen accounted for 12.7%.

### Customer Analysis
The customer base increased to 6,231 customers, reflecting growing customer acquisition and retention.

### Payment Method Analysis
UPI accounted for 42.8% of all transactions, making it the preferred payment option. Debit Card and Credit Card were the next most popular methods.

### Geographic Analysis
Maharashtra generated the highest revenue. Karnataka and Tamil Nadu also contributed significantly to overall sales performance.

### Return Analysis
The return rate remained at 4.31%, indicating satisfactory product quality and customer satisfaction levels.

